C R196 OL WF-020 | MUST | Security review requires evidence and contextual severity: investigation prompts are not automatic vulnerability declarations; rate severity by reachability, exposure and exploitability rather than mechanically by pattern, CVSS or OWASP category; avoid known false positives; mark incomplete evidence as needing verification; do not claim a static scan proves design security; do not invent exploitability; do not upgrade packages during a scan unless asked. | security review | none stated
C X30 EX WF-020 | MUST | Security findings are reported in a fixed shape: severity tag, file:line location and title, OWASP category, Evidence, Impact and Remediation; findings with incomplete evidence use the NEEDS VERIFICATION form stating what effective behavior depends on. | security review output | none stated | WF-020 requires evidence and contextual severity; the oracle does not prescribe a security report format. | A security report without per-finding Evidence/Impact/Remediation sections does not follow the workflow.

